      },
      "rev_n_3_47a801_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_47a801_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_47a801",
        "thought_text": "Use modular arithmetic to efficiently compute the last 18 digits of Fibonacci numbers without generating the entire number.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794535030.9823222
      },
      "rev_n_1_13e55a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_13e55a_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_13e55a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is inefficient and contains errors in the implementation. Instead of generating all Fibonacci numbers up to a large limit, we should generate only the necessary Fibonacci numbers on-the-fly and check for the required substring condition. This will significantly reduce memory usage and improve performance.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_13e55a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2d5a73c26e",
        "created_at": 1794535063.3222947
      },
      "rev_n_2_84523d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_84523d_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_84523d",
        "thought_text": "Instead of iterating through all possible values of b and e, we can optimize the search by leveraging the properties of the Fibonacci sequence and the given arithmetic sequence. We can start with a reasonable range for b and e based on the input values and the constraints, and then refine our search accordingly. This approach should significantly reduce the search space and improve efficiency.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_84523d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_baf9319a52",
        "created_at": 1794535130.4616911
      },
      "rev_n_3_47a801_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_47a801_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_47a801",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of checking all possible (b, e) pairs up to 2^64 is inefficient and likely to miss valid solutions due to the large search space. Instead, we should consider using the properties of the Fibonacci sequence and the given constraints to reduce the search space significantly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_47a801_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_db63e573b1",
        "created_at": 1794535214.9442835
      },
      "rev_n_4_4df434_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_4df434_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_4df434",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the search space by considering the maximum possible value for e. Since e must be less than 2^64, we can calculate the upper bound for e based on the maximum possible value of a + (n-1)d.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2551147305163680292",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794535243.1952
      },
      "rev_n_5_a3ab33_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_a3ab33_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_a3ab33",
        "thought_text": "Implement a more efficient Fibonacci number generation method, such as matrix exponentiation, to calculate F_{b+i*e} quickly without generating all Fibonacci numbers up to that point.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2551147305163680292",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794535243.1952217
      },
      "rev_n_6_8458e0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_8458e0_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_8458e0",
        "thought_text": "Use a more sophisticated string matching algorithm to check for the substring condition, such as the KMP (Knuth-Morris-Pratt) algorithm, which can perform substring searches in linear time.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2551147305163680292",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794535243.195235
      },
      "rev_n_4_4df434_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_4df434_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_4df434",
        "thought_text": "Instead of calculating the upper bound for e based on the maximum possible value of a + (n-1)d, consider using the actual length of the arithmetic sequence as a constraint. This approach can significantly reduce the search space and improve efficiency.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2551147305163680292",
